{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Scoping note on this bug's justification, recorded so it rests on its own evidence.\n\nWhile verifying AC2 of the parent incident `3276-2f81-8c75-4ddd`, the outage narrative that motivated the original treat_missing_data fix turned out to be substantially wrong: `rebar-root-disk-pressure` was NOT silent during the 2026-09-02 outage. It fired OK->ALARM 11 times on 2026-09-01, every one delivered to SNS with ActionsEnabled true, and held continuous ALARM for 3h33m before the outage — under the OLD configuration. Its 01:45 self-clear was caused by two genuine 85.0 datapoints against a `>` 85 operator, not by missing data.\n\nThat does NOT undermine this ticket. This ticket's claim is independently established and does not depend on the outage story:\n\n1. The offset-delta emission pattern in `infra/scripts/observability.sh` is verified directly in the code — every host counter publishes an unconditional delta, `0` when nothing happened.\n2. Live CloudWatch confirms dense all-zero datapoints for all eleven alarms across a healthy window.\n3. Therefore missing data on these metrics means the publisher is dead, and `notBreaching` reads that as health. That is a real defect regardless of what happened on 2026-09-02.\n\nThe strongest case here remains `mirror_out_of_sync`, and its case is now RELATIVELY STRONGER than the disk alarms', because it is genuinely silent rather than merely mis-latching: the publish sits inside a guard whose else branch emits nothing on a fetch/REST failure, monitoring_ws7.tf states no other alarm covers mirror drift, and unlike the disk alarm there is no compensating black-box probe. A live healthy host with a broken Gerrit read mutes it forever.\n\nWhat I am NOT claiming, and what should not be written into this ticket's justification: that fixing these eleven alarms would have prevented the 2026-09-02 outage. It would not have. That outage was paged and not acted on."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788401211007762001,"uuid":"e466b815-f4fb-4bbb-ab98-ddd2b7b2d978"}